MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

You can create methylDiff object with the new() function, but I do not recommend doing this. The safest way to create it is via calculateDiffMeth() function.

If you make sure the data frame part of the methylDiff object has exactly the same structure (column names, column order, column classes), then you can do the following. But I again discourage using this method because if you construct the object in a wrong way, the downstream analysis may not work.

Below, x is the data frame that has the same structure as a regular methylDiff object. To see an example of a methylDiff object, do
library(methylKit);data(methylKit);methylDiff.obj

The rest of the attributes are self explanatory, you can check the vignette/ function help to understand what they mean if you are not sure.

obj=new("methylDiff",x,sample.ids=c("test1","control1"),
                       assembly="hg18",context="CpG",
                              treatment=c(1,0),destranded=TRUE,resolution="region")

 Best,
Altuna

